      "number": 3576,
      "title": "chore(main): release 1.36.3",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-25T04:42:14Z"
    },
    {
      "body": "## Why\nMaint 82 retained two superseded closed dev-tool PRs as actionable review blockers because Maint 71 stale-close rows lacked head/generation identity and older handoffs were never reconciled after closure.\n\n## Change\n- Emit terminal Maint 71 stale-close handoffs only after the close response confirms the PR, branch and exact head, using the stale PR own delivery identity.\n- Reconcile retained nonterminal handoffs against the live PR. A closed PR on the same branch retires its old item; if its head changed, preserve the old immutable head and record the observed closed head separately without claiming the old head merged.\n- Prevent delayed same-identity actionable dispatches from reviving terminal records; dry-run closures never terminalize.\n- Document the contract and test exact-head, changed-head, open, changed-branch, and API-error cases.\n\n## Validation\n- `node --test .github/scripts/__tests__/sync_dependency_campaign.test.js .github/scripts/__tests__/sync_pr_merge_contract.test.js .github/scripts/__tests__/maint71_merge_sync_prs.test.js` \u2014 134 passed.\n- `scripts/sync_templates.sh` \u2014 already in sync.\n- `python3 scripts/validate_template_completeness.py` \u2014 passed.\n- `git diff --check` \u2014 passed.\n\nPR is ready for review; do not merge until exact-head checks, review threads and the seven-minute post-push window are satisfied.\n<!-- workflow-source:sync_campaign -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Delivery handoffs are now checked against live pull request state before they can affect campaign planning. Closed pull requests are recorded as terminal, and changed heads, mismatched identities, or verification failures are blocked from continuation.\n  * Older handoffs can no longer overwrite newer records or revive terminal deliveries. Dry-run stale closures no longer generate handoffs.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated maintenance guidance to explain handoff verification, closure reconciliation, and continuation behavior.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
      "isDraft": false,
      "labels": [],
      "number": 3572,
      "title": "fix: terminalize closed generated delivery handoffs",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-25T04:32:48Z"
    }
